From f1ec18122ec05e93df0611da585a7ed207b10009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AnnikaWU <xian.wu@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 11:34:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add dual-arm ALOHA mobile manipulator for ACT+OCS2+MUJOCO
 (ROS2 Jazzy)

Adapts the OCS2 mobile manipulator into a dual-arm ALOHA configuration for the
ACT + OCS2 + MUJOCO cube-transfer pipeline, and makes it build/run on ROS2 Jazzy.

Folds together:
- Modify for dual-arm ACT+OCS2+MUJOCO in simulation (#57)
- Add launch-time mode selection for ALOHA dual-arm configuration
- Introduce joint position tracking alongside end-effector pose tracking
- Add synchronizedWallClockLoop: wall-clock anchored policy evaluation with
  linear blend for real-robot control
- Optimize lineSearchStrategy to reduce max MPC latency
- Remove dependence on external ALOHA packages
- ROS2 Humble/Jazzy build compatibility fixes (tinyxml2 include/optional,
  declare_parameter in MRT)
